  "text_input": "60 y/o female, with no known co-morbidities, was in her usual state of health 1 week ago when she developed dyspnea on exertion, insidious in onset, gradually progressed over one week from no limitation of physical activity (NYHA Class I) to patient having marked limitation of physical activity but comfortable at rest.\nPatient complains of easy fatigability gradual in onset, progressive over the last 1 week, limiting routine daily activities.\nPatient complains of bilateral lower limb swelling since 1 week, insidious in onset, started in feet, progressed to legs.\nNo h/o orthopnea / PND\nNo h/o chest pain / palpitations / syncope\nNo h/o cough / fever / expectoration / hemoptysis\nNo h/o blood in stools / blackish stools\nNo h/o bleeding PV\nNo h/o burning micturition / increased micturition / reduced urine output / frothing of urine / facial puffiness\nNo h/o abdominal distension\nNo h/o heat intolerance, constipation\nh/o weight loss observed - loosening of clothes\nNo h/o b/l (bilateral) lower limb pain / local warmth",
